            PRIVACY
        </div>

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <p class="legal-effective">
            Effective Date: September 5, 2026
        </p>

    </div>


    <article class="legal-card">

        <section>
            <h2>Introduction</h2>

            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Rivalo</strong>
                ("Rivalo," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, stores,
                and protects information when you use the Rivalo competitor
                monitoring service (the "Service").
            </p>

            <p>
                By creating an account or using Rivalo, you acknowledge that
                you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

            <p>
                Depending on how you use Rivalo, we may collect the following
                information.
            </p>


            <h3>Account Information</h3>

            <p>
                When you create an account, we may collect:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>your name;</li>
                <li>email address;</li>
                <li>your password in hashed form;</li>
                <li>email-verification status; and</li>
                <li>account notification settings.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Rivalo does not store your account password as plain text.
            </p>


            <h3>Monitoring Information</h3>

            <p>
                When you use Rivalo's monitoring features, we may store
                information associated with the products and competitors
                you choose to monitor, including:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>competitor names;</li>
                <li>product names;</li>
                <li>product URLs;</li>
                <li>monitoring settings;</li>
                <li>detected prices;</li>
                <li>detected stock or availability information;</li>
                <li>historical product snapshots; and</li>
                <li>alert records.</li>
            </ul>


            <h3>Email Information</h3>

            <p>
                Rivalo uses your email address for account-related
                communication, including email verification and,
                when enabled, monitoring alerts.
            </p>


            <h3>Waitlist Information</h3>

            <p>
                If you join the Rivalo early-access waitlist, we may collect:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>your email address;</li>
                <li>your store URL, if you provide one; and</li>
                <li>the feature you indicate is most important to you.</li>
            </ul>


            <h3>Technical Information</h3>

            <p>
                Rivalo and its hosting or infrastructure providers may
                automatically process technical information necessary to
                operate and secure the Service, such as IP addresses,
                browser information, requests, logs, and error information.
            </p>

            <p>
                The exact technical information collected may depend on
                the infrastructure and services used by Rivalo.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo may use collected information to:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>create and manage accounts;</li>
                <li>authenticate users;</li>
                <li>verify email addresses;</li>
                <li>monitor webpages requested by users;</li>
                <li>detect price and stock or availability changes;</li>
                <li>store monitoring history;</li>
                <li>send requested alerts;</li>
                <li>maintain and secure the Service;</li>
                <li>troubleshoot technical problems;</li>
                <li>prevent abuse and unauthorized access;</li>
                <li>communicate with users about Rivalo;</li>
                <li>manage the early-access waitlist; and</li>
                <li>comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Rivalo does not sell your personal information.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>3. How Rivalo's Monitoring Works</h2>

            <p>
                When you submit a product URL for monitoring, Rivalo may
                automatically request and analyze information available
                from that webpage.
            </p>

            <p>
                The retrieved information may be processed to identify
                information such as product names, prices, and stock or
                availability status.
            </p>

            <p>
                Third-party websites can change their structure, content,
                or technical behavior. As a result, automated monitoring
                may occasionally produce inaccurate, incomplete, delayed,
                or unavailable results.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>4. Email Notifications</h2>

            <p>
                If you enable email notifications, Rivalo may send emails
                containing information about changes detected for products
                you are monitoring.
            </p>

            <p>
                Rivalo may also send necessary transactional emails,
                including email-verification messages.
            </p>

            <p>
                You can disable optional monitoring notifications through
                your account settings.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>5. Service Providers</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo may use third-party providers to operate the Service,
                including providers for:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>application hosting;</li>
                <li>database infrastructure;</li>
                <li>email delivery;</li>
                <li>security and infrastructure; and</li>
                <li>other services necessary to operate Rivalo.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                These providers may process information on Rivalo's behalf
                as necessary to provide their services.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo retains information for as long as reasonably
                necessary to provide and secure the Service, comply with
                legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce applicable
                agreements.
            </p>

            <p>
                Account and monitoring information may remain stored while
                your account is active.
            </p>

            <p>
                When you delete your account, Rivalo will delete or
                anonymize associated information within a reasonable period,
                except where certain information must be retained for legal,
                security, fraud-prevention, or dispute-resolution purposes.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>7. Account Deletion</h2>

            <p>
                You may delete your account using the available account
                functionality or by contacting Rivalo.
            </p>

            <p>
                Deleting your account may remove information associated
                with your account, including competitors, tracked products,
                monitoring history, and alerts, subject to the retention
                exceptions described above.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>8. Data Security</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo uses reasonable measures intended to protect
                information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse,
                or alteration.
            </p>

            <p>
                However, no internet transmission or electronic storage
                system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
            </p>

            <p>
                You are responsible for maintaining the security of
                your account credentials.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>9. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo may use cookies or similar technologies required
                for the Service to function, including cookies used to
                maintain authenticated sessions.
            </p>

            <p>
                If Rivalo introduces analytics, advertising, or other
                non-essential tracking technologies, this Privacy Policy
                may be updated to describe their use where required by
                applicable law.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo does not knowingly collect personal information
                from children in circumstances where doing so is prohibited
                by applicable law.
            </p>

            <p>
                If you believe that personal information has been provided
                to Rivalo in circumstances where it should not have been
                collected, contact us so that we can review the situation
                and take appropriate action.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>11. International Data Processing</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo's service providers may process or store information
                in countries other than the country in which you live.
            </p>

            <p>
                Where applicable, Rivalo will take reasonable steps required
                by applicable law when transferring personal information
                internationally.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>12. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

            <p>
                Depending on where you live, you may have legal rights
                concerning your personal information, which may include
                rights to:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>request access to your personal information;</li>
                <li>request correction of inaccurate information;</li>
                <li>request deletion of personal information;</li>
                <li>object to or restrict certain processing;</li>
                <li>request a copy of certain information; and</li>
                <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The availability of these rights depends on applicable law.
            </p>

            <p>
                To exercise an applicable privacy right, contact Rivalo
                using the contact information below.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

            <p>
                Rivalo may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.
            </p>

            <p>
                If we make material changes, we may provide reasonable
                notice through the Service or by email.
            </p>

            <p>
                The updated policy will become effective on the date shown
                at the beginning of the updated policy.
            </p>
        </section>


